WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.667
Tool calls are model-generated application input, so validate them before they reach a database, vector store, A P I,

00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:14.522
or file system. Suppose the model asks for a query and top K.

00:00:14.522 --> 00:00:17.767
First, remove unnecessary whitespace. Make sure the query is not empty.

00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:23.067
Put a sensible maximum on its length.

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:28.306
Convert top K to an integer and make sure it stays inside an allowed range.

00:00:28.899 --> 00:00:31.681
Validation is not only about syntax.

00:00:31.681 --> 00:00:34.006
Authorization matters too.

00:00:34.006 --> 00:00:40.991
A perfectly valid order I D may still belong to data the current user is not allowed to access.

00:00:40.991 --> 00:00:47.921
For example, a support agent might be allowed to retrieve orders only for the authenticated customer.

00:00:47.921 --> 00:00:50.810
The model cannot override that boundary.

00:00:51.271 --> 00:00:59.633
Treat model-generated arguments the same way you would treat input coming from an external user: validate type, range,

00:00:59.633 --> 00:01:03.129
permissions, and allowed scope before execution.
